    "notes": [
      "Repeatables mapped to slot 1 only (bank=table0/row1, investments=table0/row2, digital=table1/row1, RE=row1, vehicle=RowSubform1, other asset=RowSubform2, credit card=row1). Slots 2+ added later.",
      "433-F merges vehicle ownership+operating and parking/maintenance into gas_monthly; mortgage shares the rent line. Those registry fields are intentionally unmapped for 433-F.",
      "'*_allowed' expense columns (IRS standard) are left unmapped \u2014 filled later by the standards engine, not taxpayer input.",
      "Checkboxes (business/personal, age band, pay-period frequency) unmapped for the first fill.",
      "v2: repeatable slots added under `groups` (accounts\u00d74, real_estate\u00d72, other_assets\u00d72, credit_cards\u00d72). Input arrays fill slots in order; if no array, scalar `fallback` keys fill the first slot(s). Overflow beyond form slots is logged.",
      "v3: `allowed` section fills the National Standard food-group per-category (by household_size) + OOP (by age_band) into the *_allowed columns from 433f.standards.json. Housing/vehicle allowables intentionally not auto-filled."
    ]
  },
